# Mechanical TU split workflow

Use when shrinking a root `.cpp` by moving **behavior-preserving** method bodies into domain folders (`src/Loop/`, `src/EditManager/`, …).

**Plan template:** [`docs/Templates/translation_unit_extraction_plan_template.md`](../../docs/Templates/translation_unit_extraction_plan_template.md)  
**Legacy API retirement:** [`docs/Plans/legacy_api_retirement_tu_extraction_refinement.md`](../../docs/Plans/legacy_api_retirement_tu_extraction_refinement.md)

## Phase 0 (before first edit)

1. **Prior splits inventory** — read shipped sibling plans (`track_tu_split`, `editmanager_tu_split`, `loop_tu_split`); list already-extracted TUs in this domain.
2. **Naming pass** — table of strengthenings (action+scope per [NAMING.md](../../docs/Authority/NAMING.md)); commit with moves when they clarify ownership; **do not delete legacy wrappers/aliases in extraction phases** (see Legacy Retirement below).
3. **Cross-domain placement table** — symbol → owner TU → rationale; flag misleading names.

## Risk tiers

| Tier | Session batching | Firmware build | Native tests |
|------|------------------|----------------|--------------|
| **low / medium** | All phases in one agent session OK | **Every phase** (`pio run -e teensy41-capture-serial`) | **Once at batch end** |
| **high** | Split sessions (stop-path, commit, placement ambiguity) | Every slice | Every slice |

High risk includes: capture stop/commit, persistence gating, pre-commit edit-pass emission, cross-domain placement that could mis-file code.

## Per-phase gate (always)

1. `git commit` (phase boundary message)
2. `pio run -e teensy41-capture-serial` — **not optional** (memory/link bisect)
3. Record per-TU LOC in plan tracker

## Batch-end gate (low/med)

1. `pio test -e native` (828/828)
2. One upload offer (do not prompt every phase)
3. Optional: [mechanical split hardware smoke](../../docs/Plans/mechanical_split_hardware_smoke_checklist.md) on first split with a new model/domain

## Handoff

- User says **continue** or **stop after phase N** once at session start.
- Do not treat **behavior-preserving** as **no identifier change** — naming strengthenings in touched files are in-scope.

## LOC heuristic (review only — not success criteria)

| Band | Signal |
|------|--------|
| &lt;200 | Possible over-slice — too many TUs for one domain? |
| ~150–250 coordinator / ~300–700 domain module | Healthy (Loop split reference) |
| &gt;800 | Split candidate — only if domain rationale supports |

Primary driver: **domain ownership**, not line count.

## Naming

- **Allowed:** rename moved symbols; fix misleading prefixes; action+scope in touched files; same commit as extraction.
- **Blocked:** rename-only drive-bys; new domain nouns without user ask; repo-wide synonym hunts.

See [NAMING.md](../../docs/Authority/NAMING.md) § Migration policy.

## Legacy API retirement (move first, simplify later)

Translation-unit extraction phases **must not** remove compatibility wrappers, aliases, or legacy entry points unless removal is **required for compilation**. Prefer thin forwarders.

Legacy APIs remain until:

- all internal callers have migrated;
- tests no longer depend on them;
- no remaining extraction phase references them.

Obsolete entry points are removed together in a dedicated **Legacy Retirement** phase after architectural ownership has stabilized ([legacy_api_retirement_tu_extraction_refinement.md](../../docs/Plans/legacy_api_retirement_tu_extraction_refinement.md)).

Mark temporary wrappers with `TODO(refactor): Remove during Legacy Retirement` and `[[deprecated]]` where appropriate.
